from pathlib import Path
import pandas as pd
p=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
df=pd.read_csv(p/'results/fold_metrics.csv'); agg=df.groupby(['dataset','method']).auc.agg(['mean','std']).reset_index(); agg.to_csv(p/'results/summary_flat.csv',index=False)
lines=['# Project 2 research report','', '## Protocol','', 'All reported results below use the supplied files, mutually exclusive labels, OCD exact-row deduplication, Fisher-z upper-triangular functional connectivity for fMRI, fixed shuffled stratified outer 5-fold splits (random seed 42), and fold-local preprocessing. Hyperparameter selection for SVM/MLP is performed with inner 3-fold AUC. Each fold also stores its test indices and probability predictions in `results/*.npz`.','', '## Dataset audit','', '- ADNI: 202 samples, 186 features, four classes AD/MCIn/MCIp/NC. Aggregate MCI was excluded because it duplicates subtype rows.', '- ADNI-fMRI: 206 samples, 4,005 connectivity features, four classes.', '- FTD-fMRI: 181 samples, 4,005 connectivity features, binary.', '- OCD-fMRI: 81 samples after removing one exact duplicate, 4,005 connectivity features, binary.', '- PPMI: 543 samples, 294 supplied features, binary. The 3 x 98 grouping is recorded but no biological semantics are assumed.', '', '## Method exploration','', 'The initial candidate was CBSP using the official differentiable TabPFN prompt-tuning interface. The official example treats prompt examples as differentiable tensors, freezes TabPFN weights, and backpropagates through `fit_with_differentiable_input`. A compatible TabPFN/PyTorch runtime was not available in the execution environment, so no CBSP score is reported and it is marked `NOT RUN`. The project instead implements a dependency-light Class-Conditional Soft Prompt (CCSP). A fold-local PCA projection is frozen, each class owns K learnable prompt vectors, and prompts are optimized with class-balanced cross-entropy plus prototype-anchor regularization. This is genuine soft prompt/prototype tuning, but it is not external pretrained-model prompting. TA confirmation is required before presenting it as the course-approved Prompt Learning method.', '', '## Five-fold results','', '| Dataset | Method | AUC mean | AUC std | Δ vs best baseline | Relative Δ |', '|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
for ds in agg.dataset.unique():
 sub=agg[agg.dataset==ds]
 best=sub[sub.method!='CCSP'].sort_values('mean',ascending=False).iloc[0]['mean']; cc=sub[sub.method=='CCSP'].iloc[0]
 for _,r in sub.iterrows():
  delta=r['mean']-best; rel=delta/best*100
  lines.append(f"| {ds} | {r['method']} | {r['mean']:.4f} ± {r['std']:.4f} | {r['std']:.4f} | {delta:+.4f} | {rel:+.1f}% |" )
 lines.append('')
lines += ['## Interpretation','', 'CCSP is above the strongest traditional baseline on FTD-fMRI, OCD-fMRI, and PPMI, while CatBoost remains strongest on ADNI and ADNI-fMRI. Using the strongest baseline per dataset, CCSP changes AUC by -5.9% on ADNI, -4.5% on ADNI-fMRI, +9.5% on FTD-fMRI, +8.7% on OCD-fMRI, and +1.0% on PPMI. The 20% relative-improvement challenge is not reached under this leakage-controlled protocol. The improvements on OCD have large fold variance and should be described as exploratory rather than conclusive.','', '## Ablation','', 'The K/anchor ablation is in `results/ablation.csv`. K=4 with anchor is the fixed CCSP configuration used in the main table. Changing K has only small effects, while removing the anchor is not consistently beneficial. This supports retaining the conservative anchored configuration rather than selecting a variant from outer-test results.','', '## Reproducibility and limitations','', '- `FAILED`/`NOT RUN` status is preserved in `logs/experiment_log.json` and this report. The original torch implementation failed because PyTorch was unavailable; it was replaced by a NumPy implementation with the same objective, then the full run completed.', '- CatBoost was installed from the available package index and all five folds completed.', '- The current CCSP does not use an external pretrained encoder. It should be discussed with the instructor before claiming it satisfies the requested foundation-model prompt-learning direction.', '- The fMRI representation is a generic functional-connectivity summary. It does not infer anatomical meanings for anonymous features.', '- External confirmation is still needed for the method label and the exact course-paper positioning.']
(p/'reports/research_report.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines))
